From a06f37cef3e6366159cfa77139c971eef99900d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:39:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(2d): note the corner reliefs that get no spur

A planned corner relief whose start no pass vertex reaches, and for
which no legal detour exists, was dropped without a diagnostic. It
could leave material the operator does not expect.

inject_relief_spurs now reports each skipped relief to its caller, and
the pocket emit and avoid paths write one note per corner, named by its
XY: "corner relief at (x, y) is not cut: no pass vertex reaches the
relief spur".

Pinned by
machining2d::corner_relief_spur::tests::a_relief_no_pass_reaches_is_reported_as_a_miss;
the four-dogbones rest test keeps its no-note assert.

Fixes #3249
---
 .../src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs     | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_avoid.rs | 17 ++++++-
 crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_emit.rs  | 17 ++++++-
 crates/motion/tests/corner_relief.rs          |  2 +
 crates/motion/tests/rest_corner_relief.rs     |  2 +
 5 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs b/crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs
